.TH prof "" "Command"
.SH NAME
prof \- print execution profile
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBprof [\-abcs] [\fIprogfile \fB[\fImonfile\fB]]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
prof -- print execution profile
Usage:	prof [ -abcs ] [ progfile [ monfile ] ]
Options:
	-a	Use all symbols, not just externals
	-b	Print all bin information
	-c	Print all call information
	-s	Report stack usage high water mark
The default 'progfile' is l.out, default 'monfile' is mon.out.
.HE
.B prof
interprets the
.I monfile
produced by an instrumented run of a program compiled with the
.B cc \-p
option, and reports how execution time and calls were distributed
among the routines of
.IR progfile .
The
.I progfile
argument gives the load module that was profiled (default
.BR l.out );
the
.I monfile
argument gives the raw profile data written by that run's monitor
(default
.BR mon.out ).
.PP
With none of
.BR \-b ", " \-c ", or " \-s " given, "
.B prof
prints one line for each symbol that accumulated any time or call
count: the symbol's name, its percentage of total ticks, and, if it
was called, the number of calls and the average time per call as a
percentage.
.IP \fB\-a\fR
Use all symbols found in
.IR progfile ,
not only ones with external (global) linkage.
.IP \fB\-b\fR
Print, for every profiled address range (``bin''), the tick count and
the symbol plus offset it falls in; useful for finding hot spots at
finer resolution than whole routines.
.IP \fB\-c\fR
Print, for every recorded call, the number of times it was made and
the calling symbol plus offset.
.IP \fB\-s\fR
Print the high-water mark of stack usage recorded in
.I monfile
and skip the normal profile report.
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 12n
\fBl.out\fR	default \fIprogfile\fR
\fBmon.out\fR	default \fImonfile\fR
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ld ,
.B nm
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B prof
complains and exits if
.I progfile
is not a valid load module, or if
.I monfile
is missing or truncated.
